{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Compare **all-in, risk-adjusted costs and control**, not just platform fees.\n\nA series trust can reduce startup burdens—trust formation, board governance, compliance, and vendor coordination—and offer established servicing and launch processes. For one conventional ETF and limited budget, those savings may outweigh platform and pass-through fees. Check minimums, exit costs, service levels, conflicts, and control over branding, policies, vendors, and timing.\n\nA standalone trust offers more direct control over governance, operations, and expansion, but requires funding and managing that infrastructure. Its fixed costs may be difficult to justify for one fund, but can suit a sponsor expecting scale, seeking independence, or needing unsupported features.\n\nCompare proposals with counsel and service providers, and confirm current legal and operational requirements."}}
